backup.sh db
  ok   stdout is the file name only
  ok   name follows the convention
  ok   zip file exists
  ok   checksum is correct
  ok   zip has <name>/db.sql
  ok   zip has <name>/manifest.txt
  ok   zip has nothing outside <name>/
  ok   work directory is removed
  ok   no .part file remains
backup.sh full
  ok   zip has database
  ok   zip has source files
  ok   zip has the symbolic link
  ok   symbolic link is stored as link
  ok   extracted file is same as source
  ok   source directory is untouched
  ok   manifest has type
backup.sh source, label
  ok   label is in the name
  ok   zip has no database
  ok   invalid label is refused
backup.sh errors
  ok   fails when dump fails
  ok   no zip is created
  ok   no .part file remains
  ok   error of dump is logged
  ok   BACKUP_DIR inside SOURCE_DIR is refused
backup.sh prune
  ok   old backup is deleted
  ok   checksum of old backup is deleted
  ok   old backup is deleted (2)
  ok   labeled backup is kept
  ok   KEEP_MIN of other type is respected
  ok   file of other project is kept
  ok   unfinished file is not touched
  ok   new backups are kept
backup.sh --if-missing
  ok   nothing is created when backup of today exists
  ok   nothing is printed
  ok   no notification
